        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/g/1/castlerock-wp/barmouth-level-crossing-near-c-1.jpg",
          "filename": "Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (2) - geograph.org.uk - 213340.jpg",
          "caption": "Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (2)See C7835 : Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (1). It might surprise some to learn that the Belfast-Londonderry railway is single track for almost its entire length. The railway is about 20 miles longer than the direct road and is not too well endowed with passengers beyond Coleraine. This is the Barmouth level crossing looking towards Castlerock and Londonderry. Continue to C7835 : Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (3) (May 2012).",
          "alt": "Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (2)See C7835 : Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (1). It might surprise some to learn that the Belfast-Londonderry railway is single track for almost its entire length. The railway is about 20 miles longer than the direct road and is not too well endowed with passengers beyond Coleraine. This is the Barmouth level crossing looking towards Castlerock and Londonderry. Continue to C7835 : Barmouth level crossing near Castlerock (3) (May 2012).",
